          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "The structure of the polymers was identified by IR and NMR spectroscopy. Specifically, the IR spectra of the poly(ether imide)s revealed that the characteristic bands around 1 768 and 1 716 cm⁻¹ are commonly attributed to the asymmetric and symmetric stretches of carbonyl group of imides, respectively. The C–N band at 1369 cm⁻¹ verified the formation of the imide structure. The NMR data of the polymer PI-1 are listed in the experimental section, and the resonance peaks at 168.0 and 167.9 ppm are ascribed to the carbon of the imide group."
        }
      ],
